    "text": {
     "en": "Our chapter begins with the NIM game for two players. You played a version of it in Grade 3.\nPlayer 1 chooses 1 or 2. Player 2 adds 1 or 2 to it. They keep adding 1 or 2 to the running total.\nThe player who reaches 10 first is the winner. Play a few rounds.\nCan you win if the other player reaches 6 and it is your turn? If the other player reaches 7? Or 8? Think about which totals are winning ones.\nWinning strategy: if you can reach 7, you win, since the other player must move to 8 or 9, and then you reach 10.\nTry other targets like 10, 11 and 12 and note down the results."
    }
